1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.950
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.380
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.600
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.200
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.920
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.660
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.300
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.550
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:16.100
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.050
Stella, it’s about time.

12
00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:36.930
Mm, that it is.

13
00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.560
I feel a little self-conscious
 about being on a worldwide broadcast.

14
00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.230
Well, then...

15
00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:46.860
The break was so short,
 my coffee hasn’t even cooled.

16
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.690
Where did I leave off?

17
00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.070
You had only just introduced yourself.

18
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.740
Oh, that’s as far as I got?

19
00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:58.830
The greatest brain in the world...

20
00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.500
Punk Records.

21
00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.960
It lives on, even after your death.

22
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.130
So, is this you,

23
00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:09.920
Vegapunk?

24
00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.060
What is death, truly?

25
00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.020
Where do our ideas truly reside?

26
00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:36.320
Our broadcast will
 bring the world together, eventually.

27
00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:42.200
It will mean knowing,
 and the discomfort of being known.

28
00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:51.940
Syrup Village

(Usopp's
Homeland)

East Blue

29
00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.590
Whaaat?!

30
00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.960
If it’s not at Kaya’s house,

31
00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.470
then no one in the village has one!

32
00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:58.180
Video Transponder Snails
are quite large, you know!

33
00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:02.020
You can think of it like
caring for a gigantic pet!

34
00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:05.730
I shall put on some tea, then.

35
00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:11.320
Dr. Vegapunk played a huge role
as a leader in the world of medicine, too.

36
00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.900
I know, right?

37
00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.990
You fibber! Like you’d know that!

38
00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:21.330
This is why you need to study,
Piiman, Ninjin!

39
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.290
Then you’d know, Dr. Vegapunk is...!

40
00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:35.210
Starting in a few moments, sir!

41
00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:42.530
Twin
Capes

42
00:03:54.090 --> 00:04:03.100
Future
 Land
Baldimore
Vegapunk's
Homeland

43
00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.040
Was he born in this country?

44
00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.760
Indeed. He is the pride of Baldimore.

45
00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:19.800
Oh, the man who caused
the Nightmare of Baldimore?!

46
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:23.970
That was Franky.
He’s a ship now.

47
00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:29.420
I haven’t seen you for decades, Vegapunk.

48
00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:34.250
Birdie Kingdom

(Chopper's
Training
 Grounds)

South Blue

49
00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:40.070
Sounds like everyone’s talking about
the island where Raccoon Doggie is.

50
00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.950
The father of modern science he may be,

51
00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:47.410
but Vegapunk’s scientific expertise
helped to create a lot of weapons, too.

52
00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.350
Pirate Island

"The Wasp's
 Nest"

New World

53
00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.960
Shut yer traps, ye lousy bums!

54
00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.710
This Vega-whatever guy’s
got somethin’ to say to us!

55
00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.210
Who now?!

56
00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.760
You really think that’d get us to
let you off from cheatin’ earlier?

57
00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.970
Get on with it already!

58
00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:13.650
Can you hear me?

59
00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.580
This is Vegapunk.

60
00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:30.790
This is just an ordinary
Transponder Snail!

61
00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:33.000
World! World!

62
00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.170
Come in, World!

63
00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:42.260
He didn’t just hide it...
he was planning to deceive us!

64
00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:52.180
How dare you, Vegapunk?!

65
00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.520
Come in, World!

66
00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:58.150
Stella, the signal hijack
is one-way.

67
00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.110
I know that!

68
00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.790
Where is it broadcasting from?!

69
00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:12.710
All right! Then, without further ado,

70
00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:14.960
...let’s get on with the broadcast!

71
00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.630
Yeah! Let’s go, let’s go!

72
00:06:17.630 --> 00:06:19.710
What’s he kicking off?

73
00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:26.390
What is it?

74
00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:31.100
Go back to sleep.
Some important person has something to say.

75
00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:32.810
It is not stopping!

76
00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:35.060
Make haste, Mars!

77
00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.100
Apologies!

78
00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:41.730
Vegapunk must have taken
more serious precautions than we imagined...

79
00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:45.700
...in ensuring the broadcast
would not be interrupted.

80
00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:54.410
I do not know what he learned,
nor what he intends to divulge,

81
00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:59.880
but York said that
he assumed Ohara’s research.

82
00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:07.970
So he attempted to avoid
the same fate as Clover...

83
00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:11.010
Were you hoping to avenge Ohara,

84
00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:13.270
Vegapunk?!

85
00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:22.690
I can hear...

86
00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:28.820
...Bonney-chan’s voice,
crying out for my help!

87
00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:31.120
Jewelry Bonney!

88
00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:35.290
You shall never have the Marines’ arsenal!

89
00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.250
Get back, Bonney!

90
00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:41.710
What the hell is that?

91
00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.170
Hold on!
Outta the way, Franky!

92
00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:47.630
Sanji!

93
00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.650
Only one man gets to
score points with Bonney-chan...

94
00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.030
...and that’s me!

95
00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:15.540
Don’t think for a second that
the elderly’ll get special treatment.

96
00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.120
This is how pirates fight!

97
00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:42.190
Sanji!

98
00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.770
Stella!

99
00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.490
What’s that?!

100
00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.540
He was with the king of snipers...

101
00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.790
Restrain that thing, Oimo!

102
00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:01.960
You got it, Kashii!

103
00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:19.180
Distortion Future!

104
00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:23.650
Whuh?! She’s turned huge!

105
00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.520
What is that?!

106
00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:27.110
Jewelry Bonney?!

107
00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.110
Huh?!

108
00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:47.090
Giant-Like Future!

109
00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:58.470
I have...

110
00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.020
He’s started...

111
00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.680
...committed two sins.

112
00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.650
Therefore, whether I am
arrested or executed,

113
00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:11.610
I shall program this message
to be broadcast...

114
00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:15.700
...the very moment my heart stops.

115
00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:21.120
What does he mean?!

116
00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:25.080
Then doesn’t that mean
Vegapunk’s already dead?!

117
00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.790
Whaaaa?! Wait a damn minute!

118
00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:34.130
It was on the news just this morning
that the Straw Hats took him hostage...

119
00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.840
What’s going on?!

120
00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:41.100
Huh?! You’re kidding me, dammit!

121
00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:45.560
Here we were, doing our damnedest to
force you out of the government!

122
00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.980
Hey, whoa there!
You beat me to the punch!

123
00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:55.200
If you broadcast to
the whole world like this,

124
00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:58.240
you’re gonna ruin
the newspaper business!

125
00:10:59.530 --> 00:11:03.620
Even so, I truly want you all
 to understand this:

126
00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:08.920
Whoever may have rendered
their judgement unto me,

127
00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:12.130
I am not trying to convince you
that their intent is "evil".

128
00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.760
I will not apply the labels of good and evil.

129
00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:20.470
I know far too little about him...

130
00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:23.600
...to be able to make that call.

131
00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:26.730
Vegapunk!

132
00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:32.900
What’s that thing?!

133
00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.110
Go away!

134
00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.650
So gross!

135
00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:42.660
I have no time to waste
with the likes of you!

136
00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.460
Stop, Chopper!

137
00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:47.580
Huh?!

138
00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:51.460
You are...!

139
00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.170
That voice...

140
00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:58.510
I see...

141
00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.890
A bold hypothesis.

142
00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:07.430
The Five Elders?!

143
00:12:07.810 --> 00:12:09.900
Nico Robin, I presume?

144
00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:13.110
Robin?

145
00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:14.520
Eh?

146
00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:17.780
The woman Akainu
allowed to slip through his fingers.

147
00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.570
The man is far too soft.

148
00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.500
Protect Robin!

149
00:12:32.710 --> 00:12:34.500
Guard Point!

150
00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:45.720
We’re keeping her safe, no matter what!

151
00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:48.810
Get out of my way,

152
00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:50.770
vile insects!

153
00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:10.040
What I am about to tell you
 is so unbelievable...

154
00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:12.330
...that it might be met with laughter.

155
00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:17.300
But all of you have the right to know the truth.

156
00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:25.470
Think! Think!

157
00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:27.720
Or I ain’t gonna be a Celestial Dragon!

158
00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:30.060
I’s a Vegapunk, too!

159
00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:32.690
Where would I hide it?!

160
00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:38.440
No luck.

161
00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:42.320
There are far too many
Transponder Snails in the lab.

162
00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.820
There are no unique
Mental Waves among them.

163
00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:49.660
Tell me! What will happen
if I destroy the power plant?

164
00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:51.830
I would advise against it.

165
00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:57.840
I do not mind the destruction of the Navy ships
and crew surrounding the island...

166
00:13:57.840 --> 00:14:02.300
But we will never be able to recreate
the Mother Flame!

167
00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.970
To make a long story short:

168
00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:13.520
The world as we know it...

169
00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:18.520
...is sinking into the sea.

170
00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:39.280
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

171
00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:43.500
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop beep-beep-beep-bup-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipii pipopii, pipopiipii

172
00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:47.710
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

173
00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:50.190
Beep-bup-beep
Piipapii papipo, piipapii

174
00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:55.240
No No No No No norenai

175
00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:55.320
No, no, no, no, no, not feelin' it

176
00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:59.480
kobiritsuichatte mou odorenai

177
00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:59.520
I'm all stiff, all outta dances

178
00:14:59.520 --> 00:15:03.760
My head feels so good, 'f I get unlucky again
atama Feel so good, mata Unlucky demo

179
00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:07.860
Cola de fukitobase yowaki o
just gonna blow away the shy with a cola

180
00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:11.940
Hey all you boys & girls! Looking good!
soko no Boys & Girls! omae ii yatsu

181
00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:15.490
Hey all you boys & girls!
soko no Boys & Girls!

182
00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.460
Update failed. I've had enough!
appudeto wa shippai kori gori

183
00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.340
Wasn't it OK 'til yesterday?
kinou made nara seikai?

184
00:15:21.340 --> 00:15:27.670
La la la la la la, run, run, run...
ran ran ran ran ran ran Run Run Run

185
00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:31.390
"Hiding yet?"
mou ii kai?

186
00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:33.760
You ready yet, up for a dance
junbi wa douyo odoreru no?

187
00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:36.130
bukkowareteru kono jidai
in this broken era?

188
00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:39.810
"Come find us!"
mou ii yo!

189
00:15:39.810 --> 00:15:42.160
Spread out from here, drop into the world
koko kara kakusan sekai e Drop

190
00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:44.560
Let loose on the stage of freedom and liberation
jiyuu to kaihou no Stage e

191
00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.790
Those rising heads're punks!!!!!! No way!!!
wakiagaru atama ga Punk!!!!!! No way!!!

192
00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:48.740
Sick of waitin', goof off and dance
matenaiyo fuzaketa Dance

193
00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:50.720
Dopamine spilling over
afuredasu dopamin

194
00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:52.960
The lonely singing in unity
kodoku ga tsudoi utau koushin

195
00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:55.060
Bip-bip-bip-bup-bup-bup-bup-bupping
pipipi papapapapatteru

196
00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:57.020
Can't can't can't count me out yet
mada mada mada horobinai

197
00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.470
There's some stranger waving me over
shiranai dareka ga temaneki da

198
00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:02.210
Smilin' so wide that it can't be real
uso mitai ni waratteru
